          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
            of traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+quantum+field+theory"} algebraic quantum field theory
            or of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+covariant+perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} locally covariant perturbative quantum field theory
            – where one assigns a plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+QFT"} non-perturbative QFT
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series+algebra"} formal power series algebra
            for
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+QFT"} perturbative QFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            region (a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+net+of+observables"}> local net of observables
            ”) – fail when one considers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
            more general than
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT+on+curved+spacetimes"}> AQFT on curved spacetimes
            ):
          %p
            The nature of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
            implies that to re-construct their global configuration (including non-trivial topology as in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton+sectors"} instanton sectors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
            (see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/bachelor+thesis+Eggertsson"} Eggertsson 14
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Schenkel14"} Schenkel 14
            %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Higher+field+bundles+for+gauge+fields"} Schreiber 14
            for exposition), and hence, after
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
            of observables.
          %p
            The program of
            %em homotopical algebraic quantum field theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#BeniniSchenkel16"}> Benini-Schenkel 16
            , see
            %a{:href => "#Schenkel17"} Schenkel 17
            for survey) is to lift the axioms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT+on+curved+spacetimes"} AQFT on curved spacetimes
            to certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+nets"} local nets
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+algebra"} homotopical algebras
            such as to properly capture
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            with topologically non-trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            configurations.
          %p
            The axioms as considered in
            %a{:href => "#Schenkel17"} Schenkel 17
            have some similarity with that of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+homology"} factorization homology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causality"} causality
            condition for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+fields"} quantum fields
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifolds"} Lorentzian manifolds
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+structures"} higher structures
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+covariant+perturbative+algebraic+quantum+field+theory"} locally covariant perturbative algebraic quantum field theory
          %h2#References References
          %p Review and exposition:
          %ul
            %li#Schenkel17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Schenkel"}> Alexander Schenkel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Towards Homotopical Algebraic Quantum Field Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://indico.mitp.uni-mainz.de/event/76/overview"} Foundational and Structural Aspects of Gauge Theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://aschenkel.eu/Mainz17.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Schenkel14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Schenkel"}> Alexander Schenkel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the problem of gauge theories in locally covariant QFT
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.science.unitn.it/~moretti/convegno/convegno.html"} Operator and Geometric Analysis on Quantum Theory
                Trento, 2014 (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/SchenkelTrento2014.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                ) (with further emphasis on this point in the companion talk
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "field+bundle#Schreiber14"} Schreiber 14
            %li#Schenkel17b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Schenkel"}> Alexander Schenkel
                ,
